From aa1b1bb5b42a3338844c2d2fe96a624d5571ba39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julian Cooper <115541810+Juliansgith@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 15:12:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 27/52] Add the agent bridge (engine side)

An interface for external agents -- reinforcement-learning trainers,
neural-network policies, scripted bots -- to observe the sim and command
armies in lock-step with it. Everything is inert unless the game is launched
with /agentbridge <port>.

- moho/agent/AgentBridge.{h,cpp}: at the end of each due tick the sim thread
  sends one newline-delimited JSON message to 127.0.0.1:<port> and blocks
  until the agent answers. Observations and actions are built by a sim-side
  Lua script (/agentscript); the engine only converts between JSON and Lua
  tables, reads `wait`/`cmd`, reports script errors, and exits when the agent
  disconnects.
- Pacing: /agentspeed overrides the issue thread's sim rate (and the user
  session's interpolation rate); unpaced sessions let the sim run further
  ahead of the render loop and drain every queued sync per frame.
- Training-speed hooks for unpaced sessions: the forced Lua GC period is
  stretched tenfold, and particle emission is skipped (visual only; it uses
  a random stream separate from the sim's) unless /agentvfx.
- Watchdog (/agentwatchdog, default 60 s): a sim thread busy that long gets a
  Lua count hook that reports the traceback to the log and to the agent,
  then the process exits.
- Per-step timing (sim, observe, act, time inside Sim::AdvanceBeat).

(cherry picked from commit 6bd0e6ccf24836fc7a30084e36fca6035d92ca10)

Ported onto 8977bb9d: upstream's lua_call is the unprotected call (fba488d1); the two status-checked calls use LuaCallProtected, the old behaviour.

